{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_meet.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.remote-meet\n     2\t  \"The meeting board convention of dao.stream.remote.md (section 4):\n     3\t   none of this has a frame -- M is peers using sections 2 and 3, a\n     4\t   request and response service (section 5) over two ordinary table\n     5\t   entries.\n     6\t\n     7\t   M serves `:meet-requests`, surface `#{:writer}`, and `:meet-board`,\n     8\t   surface `#{:reader}`. A peer appends `{:meet/here <name>}` over a\n     9\t   channel whose attachment identity is its own reflexive address\n    10\t   (UDP) or a stand-in the composition supplies for any other channel;\n    11\t   M's interpreter answers with a `:meet/seen` posting on the board\n    12\t   naming the address it observed, never one a payload claimed. A\n    13\t   peer appends `{:meet/pair <name>}` to ask for a relay pair; M\n    14\t   creates two ring buffers, enters them in its table under a lease\n    15\t   (docs/design/dao.lease.md: the two identities are the subject, the\n    16\t   requesting peer the holder), and posts their descriptors, from the\n    17\t   asker's own side, on the board -- the asked-for peer mirrors `in`\n    18\t   and `out` to build its own pair descriptor over the same two\n    19\t   buffers (`dao.stream.remote-pair`).\n    20\t\n    21\t   `reflexive-tag` and `bound-gate` are the two middlewares\n    22\t   `:meet-requests`' table entry wraps: the first stamps every\n    23\t   append! with the channel attachment identity it arrived on, under\n    24\t   `:meet/from`, before the raw handle ever sees it; the second\n    25\t   refuses an append! past the bound with `:dao.stream/refused`, a\n    26\t   present answer, never silence (section 4, Bounded meeting work).\n    27\t   `meeting` composes M's own state; `step!` drains one bounded pass\n    28\t   of `:meet-requests` and answers on `:meet-board`, publishing the\n    29\t   bound's own latest decision for the gate to read. Capacity is\n    30\t   enforced a second time at grant time -- requests queued against\n    31\t   one published count cannot exceed it, each excess refused on the\n    32\t   board, a present answer the asker reads through its own\n    33\t   reflection -- and one pass handles at most `:fanout` requests, the\n    34\t   cursor preserved so the remainder waits for later passes. A grant\n    35\t   rides the judge: the complete grant fact is carried to the holder\n    36\t   on the board beside the pair descriptors, and the holder's\n    37\t   renewal medium enters the judge as a fact medium of its own, so\n    38\t   renewal is a convention path, never an injection. `reclaim-fn` is\n    39\t   the idempotent reclaim procedure a composition hands\n    40\t   `dao.lease/make-judge` for the relay-pair subject this namespace\n    41\t   grants.\"\n    42\t  (:require [dao.lease :as lease]\n    43\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    44\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as middleware]))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t;; =============================================================================\n    48\t;; The two middlewares meet-requests wraps\n    49\t;; =============================================================================\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn reflexive-tag\n    52\t  \"Middleware: an append! to meet-requests is stamped, before the raw\n    53\t   handle ever sees it, with `:meet/from` naming the channel\n    54\t   attachment identity it arrived on -- for UDP the reflexive address,\n    55\t   for any other channel whatever attachment identity the composition\n    56\t   wires. A payload's own claim about its address is never trusted:\n    57\t   the mirror step's own channel context is the source of this key,\n    58\t   never the value the asker sent.\"\n    59\t  []\n    60\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n    61\t   (fn [ctx req]\n    62\t     (if (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n    63\t       (update req :dao.stream.remote/args\n    64\t               (fn [[v]]\n    65\t                 [(assoc v :meet/from (:dao.stream.remote/channel ctx))]))\n    66\t       req))\n    67\t   :dao.stream.middleware/out\n    68\t   (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)})\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn bound-gate\n    72\t  \"Middleware: `dao.stream.middleware/gate` reading `decision`, a\n    73\t   capacity-1 medium `step!` publishes `{:meet/active-pairs n\n    74\t   :meet/max-pairs m}` onto every pass. An append! is refused,\n    75\t   present and never silent, once `n` has reached `m` -- the fanout\n    76\t   and active-pair bound of section 4's Bounded meeting work. A read\n    77\t   is never gated: the board's own retention is the only bound on\n    78\t   reading it.\"\n    79\t  [decision]\n    80\t  (middleware/gate\n    81\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/decision decision\n    82\t     :dao.stream.middleware/verify\n    83\t     (fn [d _ctx req]\n    84\t       (when (and (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n    85\t                  (number? (:meet/max-pairs d))\n    86\t                  (>= (:meet/active-pairs d 0) (:meet/max-pairs d)))\n    87\t         :dao.stream.remote-meet/past-bound))}))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn entries\n    91\t  \"M's own table entries for the meeting board: `:meet-requests`,\n    92\t   `#{:writer}`, wrapped with `reflexive-tag` then `bound-gate`\n    93\t   (outermost first, so the tag runs before the gate reads the tagged\n    94\t   request -- the gate's own verify never needs the tag, but a future\n    95\t   verify might, and the position rule lets either order run; this\n    96\t   one keeps the wire-visible transform first); `:meet-board`,\n    97\t   `#{:reader}`, unwrapped. Returns `{:meet-requests entry :meet-board\n    98\t   entry}` for a table this namespace's caller merges with whatever\n    99\t   else it serves.\"\n   100\t  [{:keys [requests board decision]}]\n   101\t  {:meet-requests {:handle (middleware/wrap\n   102\t                             requests\n   103\t                             [(reflexive-tag) (bound-gate decision)])\n   104\t                   :surface #{:writer}}\n   105\t   :meet-board {:handle board :surface #{:reader}}})\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t;; =============================================================================\n   109\t;; M's own state and interpreter\n   110\t;; =============================================================================\n   111\t\n   112\t(def default-fanout\n   113\t  \"The per-step fanout bound of section 4's Bounded meeting work: how\n   114\t   many requests one `step!` pass handles, a gap resume counted like\n   115\t   a handled request, before the remainder is left queued for later\n   116\t   passes. `meeting` takes `:fanout` to configure its own.\"\n   117\t  16)\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn meeting\n   121\t  \"M's own state for the meeting board's interpreter (never the\n   122\t   mirror's own table entries, which read and write the same raw\n   123\t   `requests`/`board`/`table` handles by the composition's separate\n   124\t   wiring through `entries`). `capacity` sizes every relay ring buffer\n   125\t   this namespace creates; `max-pairs` is the bound `bound-gate`\n   126\t   enforces once `step!` has published it, and which grant time\n   127\t   enforces again against the meeting's own live count; `fanout` is\n   128\t   the per-step request bound of section 4's Bounded meeting work\n   129\t   (`default-fanout` when not configured); `judge-atom` is the\n   130\t   composition's own `dao.lease/make-judge` state, `duration` the\n   131\t   lease this namespace grants every relay pair; `ring!` is `(fn\n   132\t   [capacity] -> handle)`, the composition's own ring buffer\n   133\t   constructor (`dao.stream.ringbuffer/create!`'s own handle, or a\n   134\t   test double).\"\n   135\t  [{:keys [requests board table capacity max-pairs decision judge-atom\n   136\t           duration ring! self fanout]}]\n   137\t  (atom {:requests requests\n   138\t         :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   139\t                            (stream/cursor requests stream/anchor-oldest))\n   140\t         :board board\n   141\t         :table table\n   142\t         :capacity capacity\n   143\t         :max-pairs max-pairs\n   144\t         :active-pairs 0\n   145\t         :decision decision\n   146\t         :judge-atom judge-atom\n   147\t         :duration duration\n   148\t         :ring! ring!\n   149\t         :self self\n   150\t         :fanout (or fanout default-fanout)\n   151\t         :renewals {}\n   152\t         :next-id 0}))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn active-pairs\n   156\t  \"The meeting's own count of live relay pairs -- reclaim-fn's own\n   157\t   bookkeeping, read here for tests and diagnostics.\"\n   158\t  [m]\n   159\t  (:active-pairs @m))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- mint-id!\n   163\t  [m prefix]\n   164\t  (let [n (:next-id @m)]\n   165\t    (swap! m update :next-id inc)\n   166\t    (str prefix \"-\" n)))\n   167\t\n   168\t\n   169\t(defn reclaim-fn\n   170\t  \"The idempotent reclaim procedure for a relay pair's lease: `subject`\n   171\t   is `[in-id out-id]`, this namespace's own grant shape. Removes both\n   172\t   identities from the table, and with them the holder's renewal\n   173\t   medium entry the grant created (dao.stream.remote.md, section 6:\n   174\t   the reclaim procedure removes the subject entries and the renewal\n   175\t   entry together) -- absent already, a no-op, so a repeated call (the\n   176\t   judge re-reaches a still-pending lease every pass) stays\n   177\t   idempotent -- and decrements the meeting's own active-pairs count\n   178\t   exactly once, guarded on the table still holding the subject. Hand\n   179\t   this to `dao.lease/make-judge`'s `:reclaim`; this namespace never\n   180\t   drives the judge itself.\"\n   181\t  [m]\n   182\t  (fn [subject]\n   183\t    (let [[in-id out-id] subject\n   184\t          table (:table @m)\n   185\t          renewal-id (get (:renewals @m) in-id)\n   186\t          had? (contains? @table in-id)]\n   187\t      (swap! table dissoc in-id out-id renewal-id)\n   188\t      (swap! m update :renewals dissoc in-id)\n   189\t      (when had? (swap! m update :active-pairs dec))\n   190\t      true)))\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\t(defn- remote-descriptor\n   194\t  [channel-id identity]\n   195\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   196\t   :dao.stream/identity identity\n   197\t   :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.remote-meet/served\n   198\t                        :dao.stream/identity channel-id}})\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn- grant-pair!\n   202\t  \"Create one relay pair: two fresh ring buffers, entered in the\n   203\t   table under a fresh id pair, both surfaces declared #{:reader\n   204\t   :writer} -- the two holders tell the buffers apart by which\n   205\t   descriptor names which `in`/`out`, not by a surface difference at\n   206\t   M, which runs nothing but mirror steps over them and never reads\n   207\t   the values inside. A third entry, one more ring buffer with\n   208\t   surface #{:writer}, is the holder's renewal medium\n   209\t   (dao.stream.remote.md, section 6): wired into the judge here as a\n   210\t   fact medium of its own, attributed to the holder, so a renewal the\n   211\t   holder appends through its reflection is evidence the judge\n   212\t   counts, and removed by `reclaim-fn` together with the subject.\n   213\t   Grants a lease over the pair's own two identities as one subject,\n   214\t   the requesting peer the holder -- the complete grant fact returned\n   215\t   here for carriage to the holder on the board. Returns the asker's\n   216\t   own pair descriptor's two remote descriptors, the renewal\n   217\t   medium's, and the grant.\"\n   218\t  [m holder]\n   219\t  (let [{:keys [table capacity ring! judge-atom duration]} @m\n   220\t        pair-id (mint-id! m \"pair\")\n   221\t        in-id (str pair-id \"-in\")\n   222\t        out-id (str pair-id \"-out\")\n   223\t        renewal-id (str pair-id \"-renewal\")]\n   224\t    (swap! table assoc\n   225\t           in-id {:handle (ring! capacity) :surface #{:reader :writer}}\n   226\t           out-id {:handle (ring! capacity) :surface #{:reader :writer}}\n   227\t           renewal-id {:handle (ring! capacity) :surface #{:writer}})\n   228\t    (let [renewal-handle (:handle (get @table renewal-id))\n   229\t          grant (lease/grant pair-id [in-id out-id] holder duration)]\n   230\t      (swap! judge-atom lease/wire-facts renewal-handle\n   231\t             (:dao.stream/cursor\n   232\t               (stream/cursor renewal-handle stream/anchor-oldest))\n   233\t             holder)\n   234\t      (swap! judge-atom lease/author-grant grant)\n   235\t      (swap! m assoc-in [:renewals in-id] renewal-id)\n   236\t      (swap! m update :active-pairs inc)\n   237\t      {:pair-id pair-id\n   238\t       :grant grant\n   239\t       :in (remote-descriptor pair-id in-id)\n   240\t       :out (remote-descriptor pair-id out-id)\n   241\t       :renewal (remote-descriptor pair-id renewal-id)})))\n   242\t\n   243\t\n   244\t(defn- handle-request!\n   245\t  [m v]\n   246\t  (cond\n   247\t    (contains? v :meet/here)\n   248\t    ;; A registration is a board record, not a lease: no lease id is\n   249\t    ;; minted for it, nothing granted, nothing judged (section 6: a\n   250\t    ;; board posting carries the lease id of the pair it belongs to,\n   251\t    ;; and a registration belongs to no pair).\n   252\t    (stream/append! (:board @m)\n   253\t                    {:meet/seen (:meet/here v)\n   254\t                     :meet/reflexive (:meet/from v)})\n   255\t\n   256\t    (contains? v :meet/pair)\n   257\t    (let [holder (or (:meet/from v) (:meet/pair v))\n   258\t          {:keys [active-pairs max-pairs]} @m]\n   259\t      ;; Capacity is enforced again here, at grant time: several\n   260\t      ;; requests may have been accepted against one published count,\n   261\t      ;; and the gate is never asked retroactively. The refusal is a\n   262\t      ;; present answer -- a board posting the asker reads through its\n   263\t      ;; own reflection, naming the ask and why -- never silence.\n   264\t      (if (and (number? max-pairs) (>= active-pairs max-pairs))\n   265\t        (stream/append! (:board @m)\n   266\t                        {:meet/pair-for (:meet/pair v)\n   267\t                         :meet/asker (:meet/from v)\n   268\t                         :meet/refused :dao.stream.remote-meet/past-bound})\n   269\t        (let [{:keys [pair-id grant in out renewal]}\n   270\t              (grant-pair! m holder)]\n   271\t          ;; The complete grant rides the posting: the holder observes\n   272\t          ;; it before acting (dao.lease.md, The holder), the pair\n   273\t          ;; descriptors beside it, and the renewal medium's\n   274\t          ;; descriptor for the renewals the judge now counts.\n   275\t          (stream/append! (:board @m)\n   276\t                          {:meet/pair-for (:meet/pair v)\n   277\t                           :meet/asker (:meet/from v)\n   278\t                           :dao.lease/lease pair-id\n   279\t                           :dao.lease/grant grant\n   280\t                           :dao.stream.remote/in in\n   281\t                           :dao.stream.remote/out out\n   282\t                           :dao.stream.remote/renewal renewal}))))\n   283\t\n   284\t    :else nil))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn step!\n   288\t  \"One pass of M's interpreter: publish the bound's current decision\n   289\t   for `bound-gate` to read next, then drain `:meet-requests`,\n   290\t   answering each `:meet/here` or `:meet/pair` fact on `:meet-board`;\n   291\t   a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the lost asks lost,\n   292\t   a resume costing one unit of the fanout budget like a handled\n   293\t   request. At most `:fanout` requests are handled in one pass --\n   294\t   section 4's bounded meeting work -- and the cursor is preserved\n   295\t   after each, so the remainder waits for later passes. Returns `m`.\"\n   296\t  [m]\n   297\t  (let [{:keys [active-pairs max-pairs decision]} @m]\n   298\t    (stream/append! decision {:meet/active-pairs active-pairs\n   299\t                              :meet/max-pairs max-pairs}))\n   300\t  (loop [budget (:fanout @m)]\n   301\t    (when (pos? budget)\n   302\t      (let [cursor (:requests-cursor @m)\n   303\t            r (stream/next (:requests @m) cursor)]\n   304\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   305\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   306\t          (do (swap! m assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   307\t              (handle-request! m (:dao.stream/value r))\n   308\t              (recur (dec budget)))\n   309\t\n   310\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   311\t          (do (swap! m assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   312\t              (recur (dec budget)))\n   313\t\n   314\t          nil))))\n   315\t  m)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/dao/stream/remote_meet_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/dao/stream/remote_meet_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.remote-meet-test\n     2\t  \"The meeting board convention of dao.stream.remote.md (section 4):\n     3\t   a `:meet/here` posting carries the channel attachment identity M\n     4\t   itself observed, never a claim the payload sent -- the whole basis\n     5\t   of punching through a restricted NAT; a registration is a board\n     6\t   record, not a lease; a meeting request past the bound is refused,\n     7\t   present, never silent, at the gate and again at grant time; one\n     8\t   interpreter pass handles a bounded fanout of requests, the cursor\n     9\t   preserved for the next pass; `:meet/pair` grants a lease-governed\n    10\t   relay pair and carries the complete grant to the holder on the\n    11\t   board, the holder's renewal medium wired into the judge, so\n    12\t   renewal rides the convention; the NAT proofs simulate: restricted\n    13\t   NAT is outbound-only and the punch is a coordinated simultaneous\n    14\t   send whose direct request-answer sequences are asserted, symmetric\n    15\t   NAT refuses the direct path both ways and forces the relay\n    16\t   exchange through the granted pair; a pair whose holder stops\n    17\t   renewing answers not-found after duration plus tolerance, and a\n    18\t   reconnect renews through the carried grant (docs/design/dao.lease.md).\"\n    19\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    20\t            [dao.lease :as lease]\n    21\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    22\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    23\t            [dao.stream.remote-meet :as meet]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.remote-pair :as pair]\n    25\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t;; =============================================================================\n    29\t;; The toy: one channel per simulated peer, to M's one table\n    30\t;; =============================================================================\n    31\t\n    32\t(defn- ring\n    33\t  [capacity]\n    34\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    35\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    36\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- toy\n    40\t  \"One simulated peer's own channel to M, `channel-id` naming the wire\n    41\t   channel descriptor -- not the reflexive address: M's own\n    42\t   mirror-step observes the address as the identity of `ab`, the ring\n    43\t   buffer it reads this peer's requests from (`address` below), a\n    44\t   value this namespace never chooses and the peer's own payload\n    45\t   never carries -- distinct per peer, exactly as two different UDP\n    46\t   sockets would be.\"\n    47\t  [channel-id]\n    48\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\n    49\t        ba (ring 64)]\n    50\t    {:channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    51\t               :dao.stream/identity channel-id}\n    52\t     :ab ab\n    53\t     :ba ba\n    54\t     :a-end {:reader ba :writer ab}\n    55\t     :b-end {:reader ab :writer ba}}))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn- address\n    59\t  \"The reflexive address M's mirror-step observes for peer `t`: the\n    60\t   identity of the ring buffer it reads `t`'s requests from.\"\n    61\t  [t]\n    62\t  (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor (:ab t))))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(defn- served-peer\n    66\t  \"M's own mirror side of one peer's toy, over the shared `table`.\"\n    67\t  [table t]\n    68\t  {:table table\n    69\t   :reader (:reader (:b-end t))\n    70\t   :writer (:writer (:b-end t))\n    71\t   :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n    72\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader (:b-end t)) :dao.stream/oldest)))})\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- serve!\n    76\t  [peer]\n    77\t  (swap! (:mirror peer)\n    78\t         #(remote/mirror-step @(:table peer) (:reader peer) %\n    79\t                              (:writer peer))))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- attacher-for\n    83\t  \"One remote/attacher over `t`'s channel, its one link shared by\n    84\t   every identity attached through it from here -- callers that need\n    85\t   more than one identity on one toy must reuse this, never build a\n    86\t   second attacher over the same physical buffers: two attachers each\n    87\t   mint their own ids from zero, and a shared wire risks one's\n    88\t   answer being absorbed by the other's outstanding id of the same\n    89\t   number.\"\n    90\t  ([t] (attacher-for t {}))\n    91\t  ([t opts]\n    92\t   (remote/attacher\n    93\t     (merge opts {:dao.stream.remote/channels {(:channel t) (:a-end t)}}))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- attach\n    97\t  [attach! t identity]\n    98\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    99\t    (attach! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   100\t              :dao.stream/identity identity\n   101\t              :dao.stream/channel (:channel t)})))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- values\n   105\t  [h]\n   106\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n   107\t         acc []]\n   108\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n   109\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   110\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   111\t        acc))))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn- oldest-cursor!\n   115\t  \"The reflection's :oldest cursor, resolved: sent, served, then\n   116\t   re-asked so the filed answer is returned, exactly the two-call\n   117\t   idiom every reflection read needs.\"\n   118\t  [r peer]\n   119\t  (serve! peer)\n   120\t  (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest)\n   121\t  (serve! peer)\n   122\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest)))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- read-all!\n   126\t  \"Drain reflection `r`'s served stream fully to `:dao.stream/blocked`,\n   127\t   serving `peer` between reads as needed, returning every value seen.\n   128\t   A blocked read is retried, served, once more before treating the\n   129\t   stream as caught up -- the same send-then-ask idiom `next` needs\n   130\t   throughout dao.stream.remote-test.\"\n   131\t  [r peer]\n   132\t  (loop [c (oldest-cursor! r peer) acc [] stalled 0]\n   133\t    (if (>= stalled 3)\n   134\t      acc\n   135\t      (let [n (stream/next r c)]\n   136\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome n)\n   137\t          :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor n)\n   138\t                                (conj acc (:dao.stream/value n)) 0)\n   139\t          :dao.stream/blocked (do (serve! peer) (recur c acc (inc stalled)))\n   140\t          acc)))))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t;; =============================================================================\n   144\t;; The meeting and its lease judge, wired together\n   145\t;; =============================================================================\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn- resolver\n   148\t  [source _fact]\n   149\t  source)\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- meeting-system\n   153\t  \"M's meeting state plus a composed lease judge over fresh ring\n   154\t   buffers, `reclaim-fn` closing over the meeting: `m`'s own reclaim\n   155\t   dissoc's a pair's two identities from `table` and decrements\n   156\t   `active-pairs`, both this namespace's own bookkeeping.\"\n   157\t  [{:keys [max-pairs duration tolerance holder fanout]}]\n   158\t  (let [table (atom {})\n   159\t        board (ring 32)\n   160\t        requests (ring 32)\n   161\t        decision (ring 1)\n   162\t        judge-atom (atom nil)\n   163\t        m (meet/meeting {:requests requests :board board :table table\n   164\t                         :capacity 8 :max-pairs max-pairs\n   165\t                         :decision decision :judge-atom judge-atom\n   166\t                         :duration duration :ring! ring :self :M\n   167\t                         :fanout fanout})\n   168\t        ticks (ring 16)\n   169\t        facts (ring 16)\n   170\t        writer (ring 16)\n   171\t        judge-config (lease/make-judge\n   172\t                       {:cadence {:ms 1} :units {:ms 1}\n   173\t                        :tolerance tolerance\n   174\t                        :resolver resolver\n   175\t                        :resolver-bindings #{:per-author-media}\n   176\t                        :reclaim (meet/reclaim-fn m)\n   177\t                        :writer writer\n   178\t                        :self :M\n   179\t                        :ticks [{:handle ticks\n   180\t                                 :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   181\t                                           (stream/cursor\n   182\t                                             ticks :dao.stream/oldest))}]\n   183\t                        :media [{:handle facts\n   184\t                                 :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   185\t                                           (stream/cursor\n   186\t                                             facts :dao.stream/oldest))\n   187\t                                 :source holder\n   188\t                                 :medium {:retention :evict-oldest\n   189\t                                          :capacity 8\n   190\t                                          :value-domain :portable-values\n   191\t                                          :attribution :per-author-media}}]})]\n   192\t    (reset! judge-atom (:judge judge-config))\n   193\t    {:m m :table table :board board :requests requests :decision decision\n   194\t     :ticks ticks :facts facts :judge-step (:step judge-config)\n   195\t     :judge-atom judge-atom}))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- meet-table\n   199\t  [sys]\n   200\t  (merge (meet/entries {:requests (:requests sys) :board (:board sys)\n   201\t                        :decision (:decision sys)})\n   202\t         @(:table sys)))\n   203\t\n   204\t\n   205\t(defn- tick!\n   206\t  [sys ms]\n   207\t  (stream/append! (:ticks sys) (lease/tick {:ms ms}))\n   208\t  (swap! (:judge-atom sys) (:judge-step sys)))\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t;; =============================================================================\n   212\t;; A meet/here posting carries the observed address, not a claim\n   213\t;; =============================================================================\n   214\t\n   215\t(deftest meet-here-tags-the-observed-address-test\n   216\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   217\t        toy-b (toy \"addr-b\")\n   218\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 100}\n   219\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   220\t        peer-a (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-a)\n   221\t        peer-b (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-b)\n   222\t        ra-req (attach (attacher-for toy-a) toy-a :meet-requests)\n   223\t        rb-req (attach (attacher-for toy-b) toy-b :meet-requests)]\n   224\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"peer-a\"})\n   225\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   226\t    (stream/append! rb-req {:meet/here \"peer-b\"})\n   227\t    (serve! peer-b)\n   228\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   229\t    (let [postings (values (:board sys))]\n   230\t      (is (= #{(address toy-a) (address toy-b)}\n   231\t             (into #{} (map :meet/reflexive postings)))\n   232\t          \"the board carries the channel identity M itself observed\n   233\t           for each peer -- neither payload named an address at all\")\n   234\t      (is (= #{\"peer-a\" \"peer-b\"} (into #{} (map :meet/seen postings))))\n   235\t      (is (not-any? #(contains? % :dao.lease/lease) postings)\n   236\t          \"a registration is a board record, not a lease: no lease id\n   237\t           is minted for it, nothing granted, nothing judged\"))))\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\t;; =============================================================================\n   241\t;; Bounded meeting work: the gate refuses past the bound, present\n   242\t;; =============================================================================\n   243\t\n   244\t(deftest bound-gate-refuses-past-the-bound-test\n   245\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   246\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 1 :duration {:ms 1000}\n   247\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   248\t        peer-a (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-a)\n   249\t        events (ring 16)\n   250\t        ra-req (attach (attacher-for toy-a\n   251\t                                     {:dao.stream.remote/events events})\n   252\t                       toy-a :meet-requests)]\n   253\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   254\t    (testing \"within the bound, the first ask's append! is honored\"\n   255\t      (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-b\"})\n   256\t      (serve! peer-a)\n   257\t      (stream/descriptor ra-req)\n   258\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (last (values events))))\n   259\t          \"the server's own answer to the append!, seen on the event\n   260\t           writer -- the reflection's own append! return is only the\n   261\t           local send's acceptance, never the server's answer\")\n   262\t      (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   263\t      (is (= 1 (meet/active-pairs (:m sys)))))\n   264\t    (testing \"past the bound, the gate refuses the append! itself,\n   265\t              present, not silent -- observed on the event writer,\n   266\t              never as a filed answer a later op returns\"\n   267\t      ;; one further step! publishes the decision reflecting the\n   268\t      ;; grant just above -- the gate reads only what was already\n   269\t      ;; published, never the meeting's own live state directly\n   270\t      (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   271\t      (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-c\"})\n   272\t      (serve! peer-a)\n   273\t      (stream/descriptor ra-req)\n   274\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome (last (values events))))\n   275\t          \"the append! itself was refused, not merely its request\n   276\t           unhonored\"))))\n   277\t\n   278\t\n   279\t;; =============================================================================\n   280\t;; Bounded meeting work: capacity holds at grant time\n   281\t;; =============================================================================\n   282\t\n   283\t(deftest grant-time-capacity-refuses-excess-test\n   284\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   285\t        toy-b (toy \"addr-b\")\n   286\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 1 :duration {:ms 1000}\n   287\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   288\t        peer-a (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-a)\n   289\t        peer-b (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-b)\n   290\t        events-a (ring 16)\n   291\t        events-b (ring 16)\n   292\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a\n   293\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/events events-a})\n   294\t        attach-b! (attacher-for toy-b\n   295\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/events events-b})\n   296\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)\n   297\t        rb-req (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-requests)\n   298\t        ra-board (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-board)\n   299\t        rb-board (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-board)]\n   300\t    ;; one step! publishes the count that still has room: both asks\n   301\t    ;; are accepted against that one publication, both queued\n   302\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   303\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-b\"})\n   304\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   305\t    (stream/descriptor ra-req)\n   306\t    (stream/append! rb-req {:meet/pair \"peer-c\"})\n   307\t    (serve! peer-b)\n   308\t    (stream/descriptor rb-req)\n   309\t    (testing \"both asks were accepted: the gate had one published\n   310\t              count with room, and it is never asked retroactively\"\n   311\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (last (values events-a)))))\n   312\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (last (values events-b))))))\n   313\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   314\t    (testing \"capacity enforced at grant time: the first ask is\n   315\t              granted, every excess one refused, a present answer the\n   316\t              asker reads through its own reflection\"\n   317\t      (is (= 1 (meet/active-pairs (:m sys)))\n   318\t          \"one grant, not two: the second could not exceed max-pairs\")\n   319\t      (let [seen-a (read-all! ra-board peer-a)\n   320\t            seen-b (read-all! rb-board peer-b)\n   321\t            grant-a (first (filter #(and (contains? % :dao.lease/grant)\n   322\t                                         (= (address toy-a)\n   323\t                                            (:meet/asker %)))\n   324\t                                   seen-a))\n   325\t            refusal-b (first (filter #(and (contains? % :meet/refused)\n   326\t                                           (= (address toy-b)\n   327\t                                              (:meet/asker %)))\n   328\t                                     seen-b))]\n   329\t        (is (= \"peer-b\" (:meet/pair-for grant-a))\n   330\t            \"the ask that arrived first was granted, its posting\n   331\t             naming A the asker M itself observed\")\n   332\t        (is (= 1 (count (filter #(contains? % :meet/refused) seen-b)))\n   333\t            \"the queued excess ask was refused, not silently dropped\")\n   334\t        (is (= \"peer-c\" (:meet/pair-for refusal-b))\n   335\t            \"the refusal names the ask it refuses\")\n   336\t        (is (= :dao.stream.remote-meet/past-bound\n   337\t               (:meet/refused refusal-b))\n   338\t            \"and why, present on the board the asker's own reflection\n   339\t             reads\")\n   340\t        (is (some #(contains? % :dao.lease/grant) seen-b)\n   341\t            \"the board is one shared stream: B reads A's grant too --\n   342\t             the refusal is what answers B's own ask\")))))\n   343\t\n   344\t\n   345\t;; =============================================================================\n   346\t;; Bounded meeting work: the fanout of one driver step\n   347\t;; =============================================================================\n   348\t\n   349\t(deftest fanout-bounds-one-step-test\n   350\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   351\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 1000}\n   352\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)\n   353\t                             :fanout 2})\n   354\t        peer-a (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-a)\n   355\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a)\n   356\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)\n   357\t        ra-board (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-board)]\n   358\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"a\"})\n   359\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"b\"})\n   360\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"c\"})\n   361\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"d\"})\n   362\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   363\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   364\t    (is (= [\"a\" \"b\"] (mapv :meet/seen (read-all! ra-board peer-a)))\n   365\t        \"one pass handles exactly its fanout: two of the four queued\n   366\t         asks answered, the drain stopped there, not run to blocked\")\n   367\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   368\t    (is (= [\"a\" \"b\" \"c\" \"d\"]\n   369\t           (mapv :meet/seen (read-all! ra-board peer-a)))\n   370\t        \"the remainder is handled on the next pass, in order -- the\n   371\t         cursor was preserved where the fanout spent itself\")))\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t;; =============================================================================\n   375\t;; The simulated network: two peers behind NATs, M the meeting peer\n   376\t;; =============================================================================\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn- nat-net\n   379\t  \"The simulated public internet between two peers, each behind its\n   380\t   own NAT, with `kind` the filtering behavior under simulation.\n   381\t   `:restricted` is outbound-only: a datagram is delivered only when\n   382\t   the receiving socket has itself sent to the sender's address\n   383\t   before, so each peer's requests reach M over the channel it\n   384\t   dialed while direct peer-to-peer is refused until both sides have\n   385\t   punched. `:symmetric` is endpoint-dependent mapping and filtering\n   386\t   on both sides: the address a peer is reachable on is a mapping\n   387\t   per destination, so the reflexive address the meeting peer\n   388\t   observed matches no mapping peer to peer and no direct datagram\n   389\t   is ever delivered -- relay is forced. Sends ride :flight until a\n   390\t   `nat-step!` filters them; a refused datagram is recorded in\n   391\t   :drops, a present fact the proofs assert, never a silent loss in\n   392\t   the model.\"\n   393\t  [kind addr-a addr-b]\n   394\t  (atom {:kind kind\n   395\t         :addr {:a addr-a :b addr-b}\n   396\t         :peer-at {addr-a :a addr-b :b}\n   397\t         :sent {:a #{} :b #{}}\n   398\t         :flight []\n   399\t         :drops []}))\n   400\t\n   401\t\n   402\t(defn- nat-writer\n   403\t  \"One peer's direct socket writer toward the other's address:\n   404\t   `append!` records the outbound mapping the send creates (section\n   405\t   4: a send may name an explicit destination from an already-bound\n   406\t   socket; hole punching depends on it) and queues the datagram for\n   407\t   the network's filter, answering ok -- outbound acceptance; whether\n   408\t   the datagram lands is the NAT's decision, not the sender's.\"\n   409\t  [net from to-addr]\n   410\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   411\t    (append!\n   412\t      [_ v]\n   413\t      (swap! net (fn [n]\n   414\t                   (-> n\n   415\t                       (update-in [:sent from] conj to-addr)\n   416\t                       (update :flight conj {:from from\n   417\t                                             :to-addr to-addr\n   418\t                                             :v v}))))\n   419\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))\n   420\t\n   421\t\n   422\t(defn- nat-delivers?\n   423\t  \"The destination peer's own NAT rule over one in-flight datagram:\n   424\t   restricted delivers only when the receiving socket has itself\n   425\t   already sent to the sender's address -- the mapping the datagram's\n   426\t   source must match to be admitted; symmetric delivers a direct\n   427\t   peer-to-peer datagram never, the source address matching no\n   428\t   mapping the destination holds toward this sender.\"\n   429\t  [{:keys [kind sent peer-at addr]} {:keys [from to-addr]}]\n   430\t  (let [to (get peer-at to-addr)]\n   431\t    (boolean\n   432\t      (and to\n   433\t           (case kind\n   434\t             :restricted (contains? (get sent to) (get addr from))\n   435\t             :symmetric false)))))\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\t(defn- nat-step!\n   439\t  \"One pass of the simulated network: every in-flight datagram is run\n   440\t   through its destination's NAT rule, delivered onto the peer's\n   441\t   inbound ring or recorded among the drops. Returns\n   442\t   `{:delivered n :dropped n}`.\"\n   443\t  [net inbound]\n   444\t  (let [{:keys [flight] :as n} @net\n   445\t        {yes true no false} (group-by #(nat-delivers? n %) flight)]\n   446\t    (doseq [d yes]\n   447\t      (stream/append! (get inbound (get (:peer-at @net) (:to-addr d)))\n   448\t                      (:v d)))\n   449\t    (swap! net assoc :flight [] :drops (into (:drops n) no))\n   450\t    {:delivered (count yes) :dropped (count no)}))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn- direct-peer\n   454\t  \"One peer's end of the simulated direct wire: `inbound` the ring\n   455\t   its mirror reads datagrams from, its answers leaving through the\n   456\t   NAT writer toward the other peer's address, over an empty table\n   457\t   of its own -- a peer serving nothing under the punched identity\n   458\t   answers not-found, an answer like any other (section 4: a path\n   459\t   exists when an answer, even a not-found error, carrying one of\n   460\t   this peer's outstanding ids arrives). Served with `serve!` like\n   461\t   any peer.\"\n   462\t  [net who inbound]\n   463\t  (let [other (get {:a :b :b :a} who)]\n   464\t    {:table (atom {})\n   465\t     :reader inbound\n   466\t     :writer (nat-writer net who (get-in @net [:addr other]))\n   467\t     :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n   468\t                     (stream/cursor inbound :dao.stream/oldest)))}))\n   469\t\n   470\t\n   471\t(defn- punch-request\n   472\t  \"The descriptor request the punch sends, one fresh id per send\n   473\t   (section 4: each side sends a descriptor request with a fresh id\n   474\t   to the other's reflexive address): the identity named is the\n   475\t   asker's own, one the answering peer serves nothing under, whose\n   476\t   not-found is still the answer that confirms the path.\"\n   477\t  [who id]\n   478\t  {:dao.stream/identity (str \"punch-\" (name who))\n   479\t   :dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/descriptor\n   480\t   :dao.stream.remote/args []\n   481\t   :dao.stream.remote/id id})\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t(defn- relay-outer\n   485\t  \"The outer descriptor one peer attaches for the relay: a pair\n   486\t   channel descriptor over `channel`, this peer's own channel to M,\n   487\t   reading `read-id` and writing `write-id` -- the same two table\n   488\t   identities the board posted, named through this peer's channel\n   489\t   (2.2: two remote descriptors naming one identity through different\n   490\t   channels reach one stream). The outer identity is the service the\n   491\t   pair reaches, because the attach probe must name an identity the\n   492\t   far side serves.\"\n   493\t  [channel identity read-id write-id]\n   494\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   495\t   :dao.stream/identity identity\n   496\t   :dao.stream/channel\n   497\t   {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/pair\n   498\t    :dao.stream/identity (str identity \"-pair\")\n   499\t    :dao.stream.remote/in\n   500\t    {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   501\t     :dao.stream/identity read-id\n   502\t     :dao.stream/channel channel}\n   503\t    :dao.stream.remote/out\n   504\t    {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   505\t     :dao.stream/identity write-id\n   506\t     :dao.stream/channel channel}}})\n   507\t\n   508\t\n   509\t;; =============================================================================\n   510\t;; restricted NAT, outbound-only: the punch is direct, after the meet\n   511\t;; =============================================================================\n   512\t\n   513\t(deftest restricted-nat-punch-test\n   514\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   515\t        toy-b (toy \"addr-b\")\n   516\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 1000}\n   517\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   518\t        peer-a (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-a)\n   519\t        peer-b (served-peer (atom (meet-table sys)) toy-b)\n   520\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a)\n   521\t        attach-b! (attacher-for toy-b)\n   522\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)\n   523\t        rb-req (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-requests)\n   524\t        ra-board (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-board)\n   525\t        rb-board (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-board)\n   526\t        net (nat-net :restricted (address toy-a) (address toy-b))\n   527\t        in-a (ring 16)\n   528\t        in-b (ring 16)\n   529\t        direct-a (direct-peer net :a in-a)\n   530\t        direct-b (direct-peer net :b in-b)]\n   531\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"peer-a\"})\n   532\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   533\t    (stream/append! rb-req {:meet/here \"peer-b\"})\n   534\t    (serve! peer-b)\n   535\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   536\t    (let [postings-a (read-all! ra-board peer-a)\n   537\t          postings-b (read-all! rb-board peer-b)\n   538\t          addr-of-a (:meet/reflexive\n   539\t                      (first (filter #(= \"peer-a\" (:meet/seen %))\n   540\t                                     postings-b)))\n   541\t          addr-of-b (:meet/reflexive\n   542\t                      (first (filter #(= \"peer-b\" (:meet/seen %))\n   543\t                                     postings-a)))]\n   544\t      (testing \"each peer learned the other's address only from the\n   545\t                board, and it is the address M itself observed\"\n   546\t        (is (= (address toy-a) addr-of-a))\n   547\t        (is (= (address toy-b) addr-of-b)))\n   548\t      (testing \"outbound-only is real: a lone direct send before any\n   549\t                punch is refused by B's NAT -- nothing lands, the\n   550\t                drop a recorded fact\"\n   551\t        (stream/append! (nat-writer net :a addr-of-b)\n   552\t                        (punch-request :a 101))\n   553\t        (let [r (nat-step! net {:a in-a :b in-b})]\n   554\t          (is (= 0 (:delivered r)))\n   555\t          (is (= 1 (:dropped r)))\n   556\t          (is (empty? (values in-b))\n   557\t              \"B observed nothing: the request never crossed\")))\n   558\t      (testing \"the punch, a coordinated simultaneous send: each\n   559\t                peer sends its descriptor request to the address the\n   560\t                board carried; both mappings now exist, both deliver\"\n   561\t        (stream/append! (nat-writer net :a addr-of-b)\n   562\t                        (punch-request :a 102))\n   563\t        (stream/append! (nat-writer net :b addr-of-a)\n   564\t                        (punch-request :b 201))\n   565\t        (let [r (nat-step! net {:a in-a :b in-b})]\n   566\t          (is (= 2 (:delivered r)))\n   567\t          (is (= 0 (:dropped r))))\n   568\t        (serve! direct-b)\n   569\t        (serve! direct-a)\n   570\t        (nat-step! net {:a in-a :b in-b})\n   571\t        (testing \"the direct request-answer sequences: each peer\n   572\t                  holds an answer carrying its own outstanding id\n   573\t                  from the other's address -- a path exists, the\n   574\t                  whole of STUN as facts on a stream\"\n   575\t          (let [from-b (values in-a)\n   576\t                from-a (values in-b)\n   577\t                ;; each ring carries the other side's punch request\n   578\t                ;; as well -- the datagrams both ways -- the answers\n   579\t                ;; being the values that carry an error\n   580\t                answers (fn [vs]\n   581\t                          (filter #(contains? % :dao.stream.remote/error)\n   582\t                                  vs))]\n   583\t            (is (= [102] (mapv :dao.stream.remote/id (answers from-b)))\n   584\t                \"A holds B's answer to its punch, correlated by the\n   585\t                 id A minted\")\n   586\t            (is (every? #(= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   587\t                            (:dao.stream.remote/error %))\n   588\t                        (answers from-b))\n   589\t                \"B serves nothing under the punched identity: the\n   590\t                 not-found error is still the confirming answer\")\n   591\t            (is (= [201] (mapv :dao.stream.remote/id (answers from-a)))\n   592\t                \"and B holds A's answer to its punch the same way\")\n   593\t            (is (every? #(= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   594\t                            (:dao.stream.remote/error %))\n   595\t                        (answers from-a)))\n   596\t            (is (= 1 (count (:drops @net)))\n   597\t                \"exactly the lone pre-punch send was ever refused;\n   598\t                 nothing of the punch or its answers was\")))))))\n   599\t\n   600\t\n   601\t;; =============================================================================\n   602\t;; symmetric NAT: the direct path is refused, the relay carries\n   603\t;; =============================================================================\n   604\t\n   605\t(deftest symmetric-nat-forced-relay-test\n   606\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   607\t        toy-b (toy \"addr-b\")\n   608\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 1000}\n   609\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   610\t        table-atom (atom (meet-table sys))\n   611\t        peer-a (served-peer table-atom toy-a)\n   612\t        peer-b (served-peer table-atom toy-b)\n   613\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a)\n   614\t        attach-b! (attacher-for toy-b)\n   615\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)\n   616\t        rb-req (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-requests)\n   617\t        ra-board (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-board)\n   618\t        rb-board (attach attach-b! toy-b :meet-board)\n   619\t        net (nat-net :symmetric (address toy-a) (address toy-b))\n   620\t        in-a (ring 16)\n   621\t        in-b (ring 16)]\n   622\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/here \"peer-a\"})\n   623\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   624\t    (stream/append! rb-req {:meet/here \"peer-b\"})\n   625\t    (serve! peer-b)\n   626\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   627\t    (let [postings-a (read-all! ra-board peer-a)\n   628\t          postings-b (read-all! rb-board peer-b)\n   629\t          addr-of-a (:meet/reflexive\n   630\t                      (first (filter #(= \"peer-a\" (:meet/seen %))\n   631\t                                     postings-b)))\n   632\t          addr-of-b (:meet/reflexive\n   633\t                      (first (filter #(= \"peer-b\" (:meet/seen %))\n   634\t                                     postings-a)))]\n   635\t      (testing \"symmetric NAT refuses the direct path both ways,\n   636\t                even with both mappings punched -- the reflexive\n   637\t                address M observed is a mapping for M, for neither\n   638\t                peer; punching is unreliable and relay is forced\"\n   639\t        (stream/append! (nat-writer net :a addr-of-b)\n   640\t                        (punch-request :a 301))\n   641\t        (stream/append! (nat-writer net :b addr-of-a)\n   642\t                        (punch-request :b 401))\n   643\t        (let [r (nat-step! net {:a in-a :b in-b})]\n   644\t          (is (= 0 (:delivered r)))\n   645\t          (is (= 2 (:dropped r)))\n   646\t          (is (empty? (values in-a)))\n   647\t          (is (empty? (values in-b)))))\n   648\t      ;; A asks for the pair; M grants, posts, and the board carries\n   649\t      (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-b\"})\n   650\t      (serve! peer-a)\n   651\t      (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   652\t      (reset! table-atom (meet-table sys))\n   653\t      (let [post-a (first (filter #(contains? % :meet/pair-for)\n   654\t                                  (read-all! ra-board peer-a)))\n   655\t            post-b (first (filter #(contains? % :meet/pair-for)\n   656\t                                  (read-all! rb-board peer-b)))\n   657\t            pair-id (:dao.lease/lease post-b)\n   658\t            in-id (get-in post-a [:dao.stream.remote/in\n   659\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   660\t            out-id (get-in post-a [:dao.stream.remote/out\n   661\t                                   :dao.stream/identity])\n   662\t            ;; B, the asked-for peer, mirrors in and out into its own\n   663\t            ;; pair end: reading out, writing in, over the same two\n   664\t            ;; buffers, and serves one stream of its own behind its\n   665\t            ;; NAT -- the service the relay exists to reach\n   666\t            scratch (ring 8)\n   667\t            b-table (atom {\"b-svc\" {:handle scratch\n   668\t                                    :surface #{:reader :writer}}})\n   669\t            b-read (attach attach-b! toy-b out-id)\n   670\t            b-write (attach attach-b! toy-b in-id)\n   671\t            relay-mirror (atom (oldest-cursor! b-read peer-b))\n   672\t            serve-relay! (fn []\n   673\t                           (swap! relay-mirror\n   674\t                                  #(remote/mirror-step @b-table\n   675\t                                                       b-read %\n   676\t                                                       b-write)))\n   677\t            churn! (fn []\n   678\t                     (serve! peer-a)\n   679\t                     (serve! peer-b)\n   680\t                     (serve-relay!))\n   681\t            relay-read-all!\n   682\t            (fn [r]\n   683\t              (let [ask!\n   684\t                    (fn []\n   685\t                      (loop [n 0]\n   686\t                        (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest)\n   687\t                        (dotimes [_ 4] (churn!))\n   688\t                        (or (:dao.stream/cursor\n   689\t                              (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest))\n   690\t                            (when (< n 6) (recur (inc n))))))]\n   691\t                (loop [c (ask!) acc [] stalled 0]\n   692\t                  (if (or (nil? c) (>= stalled 6))\n   693\t                    acc\n   694\t                    (let [n (stream/next r c)]\n   695\t                      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome n))\n   696\t                        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor n)\n   697\t                               (conj acc (:dao.stream/value n))\n   698\t                               0)\n   699\t                        (do (dotimes [_ 4] (churn!))\n   700\t                            (recur c acc (inc stalled)))))))))\n   701\t            attach-pair-a! (pair/attacher\n   702\t                             {:dao.stream.remote.pair/attach! attach-a!})\n   703\t            ra-svc (:dao.stream/handle\n   704\t                     (attach-pair-a!\n   705\t                       (relay-outer (:channel toy-a) \"b-svc\"\n   706\t                                    in-id out-id)))]\n   707\t        (is (some? post-a) \"the relay grant was posted on the board\")\n   708\t        (is (= pair-id (:dao.lease/lease post-a))\n   709\t            \"both peers read the one grant, each through its own\n   710\t             reflection\")\n   711\t        (testing \"A attaches a pair channel over the posted\n   712\t                  descriptors, riding dao.stream.remote-pair's own\n   713\t                  convention\"\n   714\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   715\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/descriptor ra-svc)))\n   716\t              \"attached ok at once, the deferred confirmation\"))\n   717\t        (testing \"the relay exchange through the granted pair\"\n   718\t          (stream/append! scratch\n   719\t                          {:relay/from \"peer-b\" :relay/text \"hello\"})\n   720\t          (is (= [{:relay/from \"peer-b\" :relay/text \"hello\"}]\n   721\t                 (relay-read-all! ra-svc))\n   722\t              \"A reads B's own stream through the granted pair: the\n   723\t               request rode A's channel to M's out ring, B's mirrored\n   724\t               pair end fetched and answered it, M interpreting\n   725\t               nothing it relayed\")\n   726\t          (stream/append! ra-svc\n   727\t                          {:relay/from \"peer-a\" :relay/text \"ping\"})\n   728\t          (dotimes [_ 6] (churn!))\n   729\t          (is (= [{:relay/from \"peer-a\" :relay/text \"ping\"}]\n   730\t                 (rest (values scratch)))\n   731\t              \"and B's own stream carries A's request: the exchange\n   732\t               is two-way, both ends writing through the pair\")\n   733\t          (stream/append! scratch\n   734\t                          {:relay/from \"peer-b\" :relay/text \"pong\"})\n   735\t          (is (= [{:relay/from \"peer-b\" :relay/text \"hello\"}\n   736\t                  {:relay/from \"peer-a\" :relay/text \"ping\"}\n   737\t                  {:relay/from \"peer-b\" :relay/text \"pong\"}]\n   738\t                 (relay-read-all! ra-svc))\n   739\t              \"the full request-answer sequence through the granted\n   740\t               pair, read from the start: B's hello, A's ping -- A's\n   741\t               own write comes back through the pair, it rode B's\n   742\t               stream -- and B's pong, with the direct path refused\n   743\t               by the simulation above; the relay carried every\n   744\t               value, the board only introduced the peers\"))))))\n   745\t\n   746\t\n   747\t;; =============================================================================\n   748\t;; A pair whose holder stops renewing answers not-found\n   749\t;; =============================================================================\n   750\t\n   751\t(deftest lease-reclaim-as-not-found-test\n   752\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   753\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 10}\n   754\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   755\t        table-atom (atom (meet-table sys))\n   756\t        peer-a (served-peer table-atom toy-a)\n   757\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a)\n   758\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)]\n   759\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-b\"})\n   760\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   761\t    ;; step! drains the ask and queues the grant; only the NEXT judge\n   762\t    ;; pass seeds it (dao.lease.md, author-grant), so the tick that\n   763\t    ;; establishes tenure-start must come after, never before\n   764\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   765\t    (tick! sys 1)\n   766\t    (reset! table-atom (meet-table sys))\n   767\t    (let [postings (values (:board sys))\n   768\t          posting (first (filter #(contains? % :meet/pair-for) postings))\n   769\t          in-id (get-in posting [:dao.stream.remote/in :dao.stream/identity])\n   770\t          renewal-id (get-in posting [:dao.stream.remote/renewal\n   771\t                                      :dao.stream/identity])]\n   772\t      (is (contains? @(:table sys) in-id) \"granted, intact at once\")\n   773\t      (is (some? (:handle (get @(:table sys) renewal-id)))\n   774\t          \"the grant created the holder's renewal medium too\")\n   775\t      (testing \"no renewal is ever appended: the holder has stopped;\n   776\t                past duration + tolerance the judge reclaims\"\n   777\t        (tick! sys 20)\n   778\t        (is (not (contains? @(:table sys) in-id))\n   779\t            \"the idempotent reclaim removed the table entry\")\n   780\t        (is (not (contains? @(:table sys) renewal-id))\n   781\t            \"the renewal medium went with the subject, together\")\n   782\t        (is (= 0 (meet/active-pairs (:m sys))))\n   783\t        (let [in-refl (attach attach-a! toy-a in-id)]\n   784\t          (reset! table-atom (meet-table sys))\n   785\t          (serve! peer-a)\n   786\t          (let [ans (stream/next in-refl 0)]\n   787\t            (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome ans)))\n   788\t            (is (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   789\t                   (:dao.stream.remote/reason ans)))))))))\n   790\t\n   791\t\n   792\t;; =============================================================================\n   793\t;; A reconnect renews through the carried grant, never an injection\n   794\t;; =============================================================================\n   795\t\n   796\t(deftest reconnect-renews-through-the-carried-grant-test\n   797\t  (let [toy-a (toy \"addr-a\")\n   798\t        sys (meeting-system {:max-pairs 10 :duration {:ms 10}\n   799\t                             :tolerance {:ms 0} :holder (address toy-a)})\n   800\t        events (ring 16)\n   801\t        table-atom (atom (meet-table sys))\n   802\t        peer-a (served-peer table-atom toy-a)\n   803\t        attach-a! (attacher-for toy-a {:dao.stream.remote/events events})\n   804\t        ra-req (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-requests)\n   805\t        ra-board (attach attach-a! toy-a :meet-board)]\n   806\t    (stream/append! ra-req {:meet/pair \"peer-b\"})\n   807\t    (serve! peer-a)\n   808\t    (meet/step! (:m sys))\n   809\t    (tick! sys 1)\n   810\t    (reset! table-atom (meet-table sys))\n   811\t    (let [posting (first (filter #(contains? % :meet/pair-for)\n   812\t                                 (read-all! ra-board peer-a)))\n   813\t          grant (:dao.lease/grant posting)\n   814\t          lease-id (:dao.lease/lease posting)\n   815\t          in-id (get-in posting [:dao.stream.remote/in\n   816\t                                 :dao.stream/identity])\n   817\t          out-id (get-in posting [:dao.stream.remote/out\n   818\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   819\t          renewal-id (get-in posting [:dao.stream.remote/renewal\n   820\t                                      :dao.stream/identity])]\n   821\t      (is (some? posting) \"the relay grant was posted on the board\")\n   822\t      (testing \"the carriage is a COMPLETE grant: status, lease,\n   823\t                subject, holder and duration, observed by the holder\n   824\t                before acting (dao.lease.md, The holder)\"\n   825\t        (is (= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status grant)))\n   826\t        (is (= lease-id (:dao.lease/lease grant)))\n   827\t        (is (= [in-id out-id] (:dao.lease/subject grant)))\n   828\t        (is (= (address toy-a) (:dao.lease/holder grant))\n   829\t            \"the holder is the address M itself observed, not a\n   830\t             claim the ask carried\")\n   831\t        (is (= {:ms 10} (:dao.lease/duration grant))))\n   832\t      (testing \"renewal carriage is wired into the judge: the grant\n   833\t                created the holder's renewal medium, a writer entry\n   834\t                in M's table, the judge's own fact medium attributed\n   835\t                to the holder\"\n   836\t        (is (= #{:writer} (:surface (get @(:table sys) renewal-id)))))\n   837\t      ;; the holder renews THROUGH the convention: a reflection on\n   838\t      ;; the renewal medium's descriptor, append, the source's ok\n   839\t      ;; observed on the event writer\n   840\t      (let [ra-renewal (attach attach-a! toy-a renewal-id)]\n   841\t        (stream/append! ra-renewal (lease/renewal lease-id))\n   842\t        (serve! peer-a)\n   843\t        (stream/descriptor ra-renewal)\n   844\t        (testing \"the source's ok observed on the event writer: the\n   845\t                  holder's bound advances on this, never on the\n   846\t                  append's own outbound acceptance\"\n   847\t          (is (some #(and (= renewal-id (:dao.stream/identity %))\n   848\t                          (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome %))\n   849\t                          (not (contains? % :dao.stream/descriptor)))\n   850\t                    (values events))\n   851\t              \"the renewal medium's append! answered ok at M\"))\n   852\t        (tick! sys 8)\n   853\t        (is (= {:ms 8}\n   854\t               (get-in @(:judge-atom sys)\n   855\t                       [:ledger lease-id :last-observation]))\n   856\t            \"the judge counted the renewal, attributed to the holder\n   857\t             by the medium wired at grant time\")\n   858\t        (is (= {:ms 1}\n   859\t               (get-in @(:judge-atom sys)\n   860\t                       [:ledger lease-id :tenure-start]))\n   861\t            \"the tenure start no renewal moves\")\n   862\t        (tick! sys 14)\n   863\t        (is (contains? @(:table sys) in-id)\n   864\t            \"intact at 14: six since the renewal, well within the\n   865\t             duration it bought -- the thirteen since tenure start\n   866\t             would have lapsed the pair\")\n   867\t        (is (= 1 (meet/active-pairs (:m sys))))\n   868\t        (testing \"the reconnect: attach! again on the pair's identity\n   869\t                  finds the pair intact, not gone\"\n   870\t          (let [in-refl (attach attach-a! toy-a in-id)]\n   871\t            (reset! table-atom (meet-table sys))\n   872\t            (serve! peer-a)\n   873\t            (is (not= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   874\t                      (:dao.stream.remote/reason\n   875\t                        (stream/next in-refl 0)))\n   876\t                \"the reconnect finds the pair alive\")))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
