{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790533000000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice7-fixes.glm-flash.report.md'","aggregated_output":"All four gate findings fixed. Files touched: only `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_meet.cljc` and `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/remote_meet_test.cljc`. `remote_pair.cljc` and `remote_pair_test.cljc` untouched (the confirmed 3.3 pair-gap, channel-loss, append-unknown, and same-descriptor reattachment tests stand verbatim). No git operations; no leftover diagnostics.\n\n**Finding 1 — capacity enforced at grant time** (remote_meet.cljc:264-282): `handle-request!`'s `:meet/pair` branch re-checks the meeting's own live count before granting; an excess ask gets a present refusal posted on the board (`:meet/refused :dao.stream.remote-meet/past-bound`, naming ask + asker) that the asker reads through its own board reflection. Test `grant-time-capacity-refuses-excess-test` (remote_meet_test.cljc:283): two asks accepted against one published count (both appends answer ok on the event writers), one `step!` yields exactly 1 active pair, one grant and one refusal, each keyed to its asker.\n\n**Finding 2 — per-step fanout with cursor preservation** (remote_meet.cljc:112 `default-fanout` 16, `meeting` `:fanout` config, step! loop at remote_meet.cljc:300): one pass handles at most `:fanout` requests, a gap resume costing one unit like a handled request, the cursor preserved after each so the remainder waits. Test `fanout-bounds-one-step-test` (:349): 4 queued asks, fanout 2 — first `step!` answers [\"a\" \"b\"], second [\"a\" \"b\" \"c\" \"d\"] in order.\n\n**Finding 3 — honest NAT simulations** (remote_meet_test.cljc:378-511): a `nat-net` model where sends record the outbound mapping, queue in flight, and a `nat-step!` filters each datagram through the destination's NAT rule onto the peer's inbound ring or into a recorded `:drops`. `restricted-nat-punch-test` (:513): outbound-only is real — a lone pre-punch send is dropped, nothing lands; after the meeting, the coordinated simultaneous punch of descriptor requests (fresh ids, addresses taken only from the board) delivers both ways, and each peer's answer carrying its own outstanding id (not-found accepted) is asserted. `symmetric-nat-forced-relay-test` (:605): symmetric drops the direct path both ways even with both mappings punched, then both peers read the board, B mirrors in/out into its own pair end and serves `b-svc` over it, A attaches a `dao.stream.remote-pair` channel over the posted descriptors, and the full relay exchange is asserted — B's hello, A's ping (riding B's stream), B's pong.\n\n**Finding 4 — complete grant carriage + renewal wired into the judge** (remote_meet.cljc:201-241, 244-282, 169-190): `grant-pair!` now creates the holder's renewal medium (a third ring, `#{:writer}`), wires it into the judge via `lease/wire-facts` as a fact medium attributed to the holder, authors the complete grant, and returns everything for carriage; the board posting carries `:dao.lease/grant` (status/lease/subject/holder/duration) plus the renewal descriptor; `:meet/here` no longer mints a fake lease id (a registration is a record, not a lease); `reclaim-fn` removes the renewal entry with the subject. Test `reconnect-renews-through-the-carried-grant-test` (:796): the holder observes the complete grant, appends the renewal through a reflection on the carried medium, the source ok is observed on the event writer, the judge's ledger shows last-observation 8 / tenure-start 1, the pair is intact at 14 (13 since tenure start would have lapsed it), and the reconnect attach! finds it alive. `lease-reclaim-as-not-found-test` (:751) extended: the reclaim removes the renewal medium together with the pair.\n\n**Lane counts (sequential, solo, under mise).**\n- JVM `clojure -M:test`: first full run showed 2 failures/2 errors — transient mid-flight churn from the concurrent slice-5 work, none in my namespaces; instructed re-run: **Ran 2,272 tests containing 183,200 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors** (focused: remote-meet-test 8 tests/58 assertions, remote-pair-test 4/14, all green).\n- Node `bb test:cljs` + `node target/node-tests.js`: full-lane failures (6 FAILs in `dao.stream.ws.browser-test` + one ws-adapter TypeError killing the autorun summary) are the concurrent slice-5 ws/rpc rework's in-flight files, identical across both runs; **my namespaces: focused run Ran 12 tests containing 72 assertions — 0 failures**, and no failures in either full run.\n- Dart `bb test:cljd`: **\"All tests passed!\" at +2140, exit 0** — my 8 meet tests (+1052..+1059) and 4 pair tests (+1131..+1134) all among them.\n\nHygiene: `cljstyle check` exit 0 on all four slice-7 files; `clojure -M:kondo --lint` 0 errors, 0 warnings; pure ASCII, all lines ≤ 80 columns; both source files remain untracked with no staging/commit/reset/stash performed.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '360,510p' && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"   360\t   answer envelope added are removed, nothing else.\"\n   361\t  [ans]\n   362\t  (dissoc ans :dao.stream.remote/id :dao.stream/identity))\n   363\t\n   364\t\n   365\t(defn- translated\n   366\t  \"A filed protocol error at the reflection: transport-error with the\n   367\t   error's name as the reason. not-found marks the reflection gone at\n   368\t   filing; no-surface and oversize mark nothing.\"\n   369\t  [e]\n   370\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   371\t   :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t(defn- learn!\n   375\t  \"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\n   376\t   surface, plus :closable.\"\n   377\t  [refl answer]\n   378\t  (swap! refl assoc\n   379\t         :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\n   380\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n   381\t                        :closable)))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- install-more!\n   385\t  \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n   386\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n   387\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n   388\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n   389\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n   390\t   its own stream.\"\n   391\t  [link answer]\n   392\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\n   393\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n   394\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\n   395\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\n   396\t        (let [[o & further] more]\n   397\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\n   398\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- absorb!\n   402\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   403\t   id is outstanding is taken: a not-found error marks the reflection\n   404\t   gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's descriptor and\n   405\t   declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is emitted on the\n   406\t   event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is filed under its\n   407\t   id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose id is not\n   408\t   outstanding, and values that are not well-formed answers, are\n   409\t   dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   410\t  [link v]\n   411\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   412\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   413\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   414\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   415\t              req (:req entry)\n   416\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   417\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   418\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   419\t          (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   420\t          (cond\n   421\t            (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   422\t            (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   423\t                (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   424\t                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   425\t                  (emit! link v)))\n   426\t\n   427\t            (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   428\t            ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   429\t            ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   430\t            (when (nil? e)\n   431\t              (learn! refl v)\n   432\t              (emit! link v))\n   433\t\n   434\t            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   435\t            (emit! link v)\n   436\t\n   437\t            :else\n   438\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   439\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   440\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\n   441\t\n   442\t\n   443\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   444\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   445\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   446\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   447\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   448\t  [link]\n   449\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   450\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   451\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   452\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   453\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   454\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   455\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn- retry-pending!\n   459\t  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n   460\t   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n   461\t   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n   462\t  [link]\n   463\t  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n   464\t    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n   465\t\n   466\t\n   467\t(defn- drain!\n   468\t  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n   469\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n   470\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n   471\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n   472\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n   473\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n   474\t   one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n   475\t   is accepted.\"\n   476\t  [link]\n   477\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   478\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n   479\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n   480\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n   481\t    (retry-pending! link)\n   482\t    (loop []\n   483\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\n   484\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   485\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   486\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\n   487\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   488\t              (recur))\n   489\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   490\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n   491\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   492\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\n   493\t          nil)))))\n   494\t\n   495\t\n   496\t;; =============================================================================\n   497\t;; The reflection (2.4)\n   498\t;; =============================================================================\n   499\t\n   500\t(defn- result\n   501\t  [outcome]\n   502\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n   503\t\n   504\t\n   505\t(defn- refl-descriptor\n   506\t  \"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\n   507\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\n   508\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\n   509\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\n   510\t   channel loss.\"\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware\n     2\t  \"DaoStream middleware: a handle-level adapter value, one `in` transform\n     3\t   over the operation map and one `out` transform over the outcome map\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md).\n     5\t\n     6\t   A middleware is a value, never a callback: every transform here is\n     7\t   called downward by the caller and returns at once. `wrap` composes a\n     8\t   chain over a handle; `apply-request` is the one place an operation map\n     9\t   becomes a protocol call; `gate` and `present` are the two generic\n    10\t   middlewares; `encryption` and `metering` are the spec's exemplars;\n    11\t   `channel-allow-list` is the trivial policy this repository ships with.\n    12\t\n    13\t   The position rule is structural, not a convention: `wrap` validates\n    14\t   every `out` result against the permitted changes and raises on a\n    15\t   violation, so a filter cannot be expressed. Each transform is still\n    16\t   total, returns at once, never loops, retries, waits or touches the\n    17\t   inner handle, and maps inner position p to outer position p.\"\n    18\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t;; =============================================================================\n    22\t;; The one dispatch point\n    23\t;; =============================================================================\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn- dispatch\n    26\t  \"Apply one operation map to a plain handle: the place an operation map\n    27\t   becomes a protocol call. An op outside the middleware vocabulary\n    28\t   (cursor, next, append!) is a defect in the host's own assembly -- the\n    29\t   mirror validates ops before this -- so it throws, per the contract's\n    30\t   reservation of exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention).\"\n    31\t  [h req]\n    32\t  (let [[arg] (:dao.stream.remote/args req)]\n    33\t    (case (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n    34\t      :dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h arg)\n    35\t      :dao.stream/next (stream/next h arg)\n    36\t      :dao.stream/append! (stream/append! h arg)\n    37\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: unknown operation\"\n    38\t                      {:op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)})))))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defprotocol IMiddlewareHandle\n    42\t  \"Internal seam of this namespace: the handle `wrap` returns answers one\n    43\t   whole chain pass under a caller-supplied context. `apply-request` uses\n    44\t   it so a composition (the mirror step of dao.stream.remote.md) can run\n    45\t   a table entry's middleware with its own context, exactly as the\n    46\t   wrapped handle's protocol methods run it with the local caller's {}.\n    47\t   Call `apply-request`, never this.\"\n    48\t\n    49\t  (operate-through\n    50\t    [handle ctx req]\n    51\t    \"Run the wrapped chain for operation map `req` under `ctx`.\"))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn apply-request\n    55\t  \"Applies one operation map to a handle: `(apply-request h ctx req) ->\n    56\t   outcome`. On a plain handle this is the protocol call and `ctx` is\n    57\t   unused. On a handle `wrap` returned, this is the whole chain pass\n    58\t   under `ctx`: the entry point the mirror step composes with a channel\n    59\t   context. Extra qualified keys on `req` pass through untouched.\"\n    60\t  [h ctx req]\n    61\t  (if (satisfies? IMiddlewareHandle h)\n    62\t    (operate-through h ctx req)\n    63\t    (dispatch h req)))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t;; =============================================================================\n    67\t;; wrap\n    68\t;; =============================================================================\n    69\t\n    70\t(def ^:private position-keys\n    71\t  \"The outcome keys an `out` result may never change: the outcome kind,\n    72\t   the stream identity, and every key naming the operation, the request\n    73\t   id or a position -- a cursor, an anchor or a gap recovery cursor.\n    74\t   Adding any of these where the outcome had none is a change too.\"\n    75\t  [:dao.stream/outcome\n    76\t   :dao.stream/cursor\n    77\t   :dao.stream/anchor\n    78\t   :dao.stream/identity\n    79\t   :dao.stream.remote/op\n    80\t   :dao.stream.remote/id])\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- position-preserving?\n    84\t  \"True when `result`, the outcome an `out` transform returns for the\n    85\t   `outcome` it received, makes none of the changes the position rule\n    86\t   forbids: no key of the outcome is dropped, the outcome kind, the\n    87\t   identity, the operation, the request id and every cursor, anchor and\n    88\t   gap recovery cursor are unchanged, and -- except for `next`'s\n    89\t   :dao.stream/value on :dao.stream/ok, the one replacement a value\n    90\t   transform owns -- the value is unchanged. Open keys may be added.\n    91\t   Structural checks over the two outcome maps only, never a walk over\n    92\t   elements.\"\n    93\t  [req outcome result]\n    94\t  (and (map? result)\n    95\t       (every? #(contains? result %) (keys outcome))\n    96\t       (every? (fn [k]\n    97\t                 (and (= (contains? outcome k) (contains? result k))\n    98\t                      (= (get outcome k) (get result k))))\n    99\t               position-keys)\n   100\t       (let [value-allowed? (and (= :dao.stream/next\n   101\t                                    (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   102\t                                 (= :dao.stream/ok\n   103\t                                    (:dao.stream/outcome result)))]\n   104\t         (or value-allowed?\n   105\t             (and (= (contains? outcome :dao.stream/value)\n   106\t                     (contains? result :dao.stream/value))\n   107\t                  (= (get outcome :dao.stream/value)\n   108\t                     (get result :dao.stream/value)))))))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn- run-outs\n   112\t  \"Run every `out` transform from the innermost outward over `outcome`,\n   113\t   for the middlewares at chain indices below `upto`. Each result is\n   114\t   validated against the position rule: an `out` that changes anything\n   115\t   beyond the permitted replacements is a defect in the host's own\n   116\t   assembly of the chain and raises, per the contract's reservation of\n   117\t   exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention) -- a filter is then\n   118\t   impossible, not merely discouraged.\"\n   119\t  [chain ctx req outcome upto]\n   120\t  (reduce\n   121\t    (fn [out i]\n   122\t      (let [result ((:dao.stream.middleware/out (nth chain i))\n   123\t                    ctx req out)]\n   124\t        (if (position-preserving? req out result)\n   125\t          result\n   126\t          (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: out broke the position rule\"\n   127\t                          {:middleware i\n   128\t                           :op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   129\t                           :received out\n   130\t                           :returned result})))))\n   131\t    outcome\n   132\t    (range (dec upto) -1 -1)))\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t(defn- operate\n   136\t  \"One pass of `chain` over `req` under `ctx`: every `in` from the\n   137\t   outermost inward, the final request applied to `h` with\n   138\t   `apply-request` (which recurses into an inner wrapped handle, so\n   139\t   `ctx` carries through nesting), every `out` from the innermost\n   140\t   outward. An `in` answering an outcome map short-circuits: the inner\n   141\t   handle is not consulted and only the middlewares outside it\n   142\t   transform the outcome.\"\n   143\t  [h chain ctx req]\n   144\t  (loop [i 0, req req]\n   145\t    (if (= i (count chain))\n   146\t      (run-outs chain ctx req (apply-request h ctx req) (count chain))\n   147\t      (let [res ((:dao.stream.middleware/in (nth chain i)) ctx req)]\n   148\t        (if (stream/outcome-map? res)\n   149\t          (run-outs chain ctx req res i)\n   150\t          (recur (inc i) res))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- instantiated\n   154\t  \"Instantiate one middleware of a chain at wrap: when its definition\n   155\t   declares a `:dao.stream.middleware/state` constructor, `wrap` calls\n   156\t   it once, here, and specializes the definition's transforms to the\n   157\t   state minted. The state is therefore state of the wrapped handle --\n   158\t   one definition wrapped over two handles holds two states, each\n   159\t   minted by its own wrap (dao.stream.middleware.md, gate). A\n   160\t   definition that declares no constructor wraps as it is.\"\n   161\t  [mw]\n   162\t  (if-some [make (:dao.stream.middleware/state mw)]\n   163\t    (let [s (make)]\n   164\t      {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   165\t       (fn [ctx req] ((:dao.stream.middleware/in mw) s ctx req))\n   166\t       :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   167\t       (fn [ctx req out] ((:dao.stream.middleware/out mw) s ctx req out))})\n   168\t    mw))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn wrap\n   172\t  \"Compose `chain`, a vector of middleware values applied outermost\n   173\t   first, over handle `h`. The returned handle implements exactly the\n   174\t   protocols `h` implements -- descriptor, which every handle carries,\n   175\t   plus its reader, writer and closable surfaces. On each protocol call\n   176\t   it builds the operation map, runs every `in` outermost inward,\n   177\t   applies the result to `h` with `apply-request` under the local\n   178\t   caller's {} context, and runs every `out` innermost outward, each\n   179\t   `out` result validated against the position rule -- a result beyond\n   180\t   the permitted changes raises, so a filter cannot hide in a chain.\n   181\t   `wrap` also mints each middleware definition's declared state once,\n   182\t   here, so that state belongs to this wrapped handle. `descriptor` and\n   183\t   `close!` delegate to `h` unchanged: no middleware sees them. The\n   184\t   surface branches below are plain reify forms, one per combination,\n   185\t   because a handle implements its surface and no other.\"\n   186\t  [h chain]\n   187\t  (let [chain (mapv instantiated chain)\n   188\t        flow (fn [ctx req] (operate h chain ctx req))\n   189\t        r? (stream/reader? h)\n   190\t        w? (stream/writer? h)\n   191\t        c? (stream/closable? h)]\n   192\t    (cond\n   193\t      (and r? w? c?)\n   194\t      (reify\n   195\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   196\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   200\t\n   201\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   205\t\n   206\t        (cursor\n   207\t          [_ anchor]\n   208\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   209\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   210\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
